== 2.3 Hydration and Food Safety

Safe drinking water is important throughout the day and during activity. Requirements vary with the person, environment and exertion; thirst and urine colour can offer clues but are not diagnostic tests by themselves. A person with vomiting, severe dehydration, confusion or other concerning symptoms may require prompt clinical care. Avoid presenting a fixed fluid volume as correct for everyone.

Food can become contaminated by microorganisms or harmful substances. Wash hands and food-contact surfaces, keep raw foods separate from ready-to-eat foods, cook thoroughly, and store perishable foods at safe temperatures. Use safe water and ingredients. A food may be unsafe without looking or smelling unusual; when in doubt, follow reliable local food-safety guidance. Never assume reheating makes every unsafe food safe.

#concept-box("Prevent cross-contamination")[
  Using the same unwashed knife for raw meat and ready-to-eat vegetables can transfer microorganisms. Clean the equipment and separate raw and ready-to-eat foods.
]

== 2.4 Reading a Label

Check the serving size before interpreting nutrient quantities. If a label gives 4 grams of sugar per serving and a package contains three servings, consuming the entire package would provide 4 × 3 = 12 grams according to the label. The calculation does not establish whether an individual diet is healthy, and labels and serving conventions can vary.

#worked-example(1, "A nutrient function", tier: "FOUNDATION",
  [Which nutrient group supplies amino acids used in growth and repair? \
A. Protein \
B. Water only \
C. Dietary fibre only \
D. Sodium chloride only],
  [Protein supplies amino acids for tissue maintenance and many other functions. The answer is *A*.])
#worked-example(2, "Foods contain mixtures", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [Which statement about beans is most accurate? \
A. They contain protein and no other nutrients \
B. They can contribute protein, carbohydrate and fibre \
C. They are a mineral supplement only \
D. They cannot form part of a varied diet],
  [Beans contain several nutrients; categories do not imply exclusivity. The answer is *B*.])
#worked-example(3, "Prevent contamination", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [A cook has cut raw chicken and now wants to prepare a salad. What should happen first? \
A. Use the same unwashed board immediately \
B. Wipe the board with a dry hand only \
C. Clean equipment and separate raw food from ready-to-eat food \
D. Assume all raw food is sterile],
  [Cleaning and separation reduce the opportunity for cross-contamination. The answer is *C*.])
#worked-example(4, "Label calculation", tier: "JAMB CHALLENGE",
  [A packet contains 3 servings. Each serving has 4 g of sugar. How much sugar is in the whole packet according to the label? \
A. 1 g \
B. 4 g \
C. 7 g \
D. 12 g],
  [Multiply the amount per serving by the number of servings: 4 × 3 = 12 g. The answer is *D*.])

#trap-box("Read the quantity")[
  A figure per serving is not automatically the amount in the whole package. Also distinguish adult population guidance from a prescription for every person.
]

